# Shrinks a just-recorded obstacle polygon inward by the chassis half-width.
#
# RecordArea (mowgli_behavior) records base_footprint's own trajectory while
# the operator drives around the obstacle. Tracing an obstacle by driving the
# chassis EDGE along it — the natural way to do it — means the recorded
# vertex sits chassis_width/2 further from the true physical surface than the
# operator intended, on whichever side was away from the object at that
# point. Left uncorrected, EVERY obstacle recorded this way is drawn larger
# than reality by roughly that margin all the way round, on top of whatever
# obstacle_margin later adds for planning.
#
# This is a PHYSICAL correction only: it uses the raw chassis half-width
# (robot_width/2), never obstacle_margin or the +0.05 m planning footprint
# margin used elsewhere (root CLAUDE.md's "count the body exactly once"
# table) — those are planning clearances, not a measurement of where the
# body's edge actually is.
#
# Erosion can collapse a small/thin polygon entirely; that is reported as
# success=false with a message, never as a silently-uncorrected polygon —
# the whole point is that the software must not leave extra room in.
geometry_msgs/Polygon polygon
---
geometry_msgs/Polygon corrected
bool success
string message
